; An exec in the style of MM2: one step adds the templates of every match of
; its patterns, each matched against the state the step starts from, and
; removes the exec row.  Here the rule is declared and the (exec close) row
; starts it; in MM2 the exec row carries its rule, and tcalc@0.1 has no rules
; held by the state.  The count is a check, not a read, so the member that
; takes the exec row is jointly enabled with the members that ask for it.
; Under every the step adds (edge a c) and (edge b d), and not (edge a d),
; which only the new edges give.  One match at a time also reaches the
; partial and the longer closures, as the exec is removed earlier or later.
(store set)
(edge a b)
(edge b c)
(edge c d)
(exec close)
(rule close (read (edge $x $y) (edge $y $z)) (count 1 (exec close)) (make (edge $x $z)))
(rule done (take (exec close)))
